SUMMARY:Deadline 11:00 UK — Knowledge Transfer Partnership: 2026 to 202
 7 round 4 (Innovate UK)
DESCRIPTION:Innovate UK funds a university-led partnership placing a grad
 uate associate in a UK business for an innovation project\, part-funded 
 by the business.\n\nEffort: heavy (6-8 weeks part-time).\n\nWhat you nee
 d:\n• Business partner commitment — UK firm with at least two full-t
 ime employees\; cash contribution required\n• KTP adviser engagement 
 — Expression of interest and adviser approval — typical\, confirm in
  the guidance\n• University KTP office approval — Internal costing a
 nd sign-off — typical\, confirm in the guidance\n• Project plan and 
 workplan — Objectives\, milestones and associate tasks — typical\, c
 onfirm in the guidance\n• Budget and contribution breakdown — SMEs u
 sually pay about a third\; large firms half — confirm in the guidance\
 n• Academic supervision commitment — About half a day per week of su
 pervisor time — typical\, confirm in the guidance\n• IFS application
  submission — Online form on the Innovation Funding Service\n\nhttps:/
 /www.ukri.org/opportunity/knowledge-transfer-partnership-2026-to-2027-ro
 und-4/
URL:https://www.ukri.org/opportunity/knowledge-transfer-partnership-2026-
 to-2027-round-4/
