DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270219
SUMMARY:Deadline 16:00 UK — Early Career Fellowships (Leverhulme Trust)
DESCRIPTION:Three-year postdoctoral fellowship in any discipline for rese
 archers within about four years of submitting their doctorate\, co-funde
 d by the Leverhulme Trust and the host university\; around 145 awards ar
 e expected in 2027.\n\nEffort: moderate (3-5 days over 6-8 weeks).\n\nWh
 at you need:\n• Eligible candidate — Thesis submitted within four ye
 ars of the deadline\; fewer than three years of own-research postdoctora
 l posts\; UK degree or UK academic post.\n• Departmental matching-fund
 ing commitment — Must be identified and secured before the closing dat
 e from general university funds (not another grant) and allocated to the
  named individual.\n• Head of department / host statement — Typical\
 ; confirm the format in the 2027 guidance for applicants.\n• Candidate
 's research proposal and CV — Typical\; confirm limits in the 2027 app
 lication help notes.\n• Referees — Typical\; confirm number in the h
 elp notes.\n• University approval — The host university approves and
  submits the application by 4pm on the closing date.\n\nhttps://www.leve
 rhulme.ac.uk/early-career-fellowships
URL:https://www.leverhulme.ac.uk/early-career-fellowships
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Deadline 16:00 UK — Early Career Fellowships (Leverhulme Tr
 ust)
TRIGGER:-P7D
END:VALARM
