BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:scheme-royal-society-research-grants-deadline@wave-research
DTSTAMP:20261123T121712Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270325
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270326
SUMMARY:Deadline — Research Grants (Royal Society)
DESCRIPTION:Seed-corn grant of up to £30\,000 for up to 12 months for ne
 wly independent researchers to buy specialised equipment and consumables
  and to fund essential fieldwork travel.\n\nEffort: moderate (2-3 weeks 
 part-time).\n\nWhat you need:\n• Evidence of independent status — Fu
 ll list of positions showing when you became independent\; Annex 1 of th
 e scheme notes gives examples of eligible posts.\n• Lay summary and sc
 ientific abstract — Lay summary max 250 words\; a scientific abstract 
 is now also required.\n• Research proposal — 1\,000 words in the for
 m or a PDF of up to 2 pages of A4 (Arial 10 or larger\, under 3MB).\n•
  Relevance to earlier work — Max 200 words.\n• How the proposal diff
 ers from current research — Max 500 words\, including confirmation tha
 t it does not supplement ongoing research or existing grants and that yo
 u will lead.\n• Rationale and motivation — Max 250 words\, including
  how the award helps secure future funding.\n• Collaborations — Max 
 500 words.\n• Justification of expenses and equipment — Full justifi
 cation of every consumable\, travel and equipment item\, with supplier q
 uotations uploaded as PDF. A Head of Department letter is needed only wh
 ere shared-use equipment requires confirmed priority access.\n• Data m
 anagement and sharing plan — Max 200 words.\n• No Head of Department
  statement or referee — Not required for this scheme\; CVs and support
 ing letters are not accepted.\n\nhttps://royalsociety.org/grants/researc
 h-grants/
URL:https://royalsociety.org/grants/research-grants/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Deadline — Research Grants (Royal Society)
TRIGGER:-P7D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
