DESCRIPTION:Effort: moderate (2-3 weeks part-time).\n\nWhat you need:\n
 • Evidence of independent status — Full list of positions showing wh
 en you became independent\; Annex 1 of the scheme notes gives examples o
 f eligible posts.\n• Lay summary and scientific abstract — Lay summa
 ry max 250 words\; a scientific abstract is now also required.\n• Rese
 arch proposal — 1\,000 words in the form or a PDF of up to 2 pages of 
 A4 (Arial 10 or larger\, under 3MB).\n• Relevance to earlier work — 
 Max 200 words.\n• How the proposal differs from current research — M
 ax 500 words\, including confirmation that it does not supplement ongoin
 g research or existing grants and that you will lead.\n• Rationale and
  motivation — Max 250 words\, including how the award helps secure fut
 ure funding.\n• Collaborations — Max 500 words.\n• Justification o
 f expenses and equipment — Full justification of every consumable\, tr
 avel and equipment item\, with supplier quotations uploaded as PDF. A He
 ad of Department letter is needed only where shared-use equipment requir
 es confirmed priority access.\n• Data management and sharing plan — 
 Max 200 words.\n• No Head of Department statement or referee — Not r
 equired for this scheme\; CVs and supporting letters are not accepted.\n
 \nhttps://royalsociety.org/grants/research-grants/
