BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eu-HORIZON-CL5-2027-02-D3-09-deadline@wave-research
DTSTAMP:20261123T121712Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline — Innovative technologies and solutions to improve wav
 e and tidal energy systems (Horizon Europe)
DESCRIPTION:A single Horizon Europe Innovation Action of about €43 mill
 ion to develop\, validate and demonstrate wave and tidal energy technolo
 gy\, covering survival in harsh seas\, moorings\, foundations\, conditio
 n monitoring and the use of AI. It opens on 3 December 2026 and closes o
 n 31 March 2027\; you would join as a partner rather than lead.\n\nEffor
 t: moderate (2-3 weeks of your time).\n\nWhat you need:\n• A place in 
 a consortium — Only one grant is expected\; find out who is coordinati
 ng a bid and offer a defined contribution before partner lists close\n
 • One-page statement of what you bring — For example survivability a
 nd wave-loading modelling\, tank testing or AI methods\, mapped to the b
 reakthrough\, validation or demonstration challenge\n• Your tasks in t
 he work plan — Text for the coordinator on your tasks\, deliverables a
 nd effort\; the whole proposal is limited to 60 pages for this topic\n
 • Partner profile and key staff — Organisation description\, relevan
 t projects and facilities for the application form\; typical — confirm
  in the guidance\n• Budget for Manchester's share — Staff effort and
  costs agreed with the coordinator and your research office\; typical 
 — confirm in the guidance\n• Institutional registration and sign-off
  — Manchester's research office approves participation and costs\; typ
 ical — confirm in the guidance\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-te
 nders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/HORIZON-CL
 5-2027-02-D3-09
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen
 /opportunities/topic-details/HORIZON-CL5-2027-02-D3-09
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Deadline — Innovative technologies and solutions to improve
  wave and tidal energy systems (Horizon Europe)
TRIGGER:-P7D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
