BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:scheme-royal-society-short-industry-fellowship-deadline@wave-research
DTSTAMP:20261123T121712Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270527
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270528
SUMMARY:Deadline — Short Industry Fellowship (Royal Society)
DESCRIPTION:Short secondment (3-6 months full-time\, or 50% for up to 12 
 months) for an academic and/or their postdoctoral researcher to work on 
 a joint project with a UK company\; covers basic salary during the secon
 dment plus up to £1\,000 research expenses.\n\nEffort: moderate (3-5 we
 eks elapsed).\n\nWhat you need:\n• UK industry partner — Company wit
 h an established research team and facilities\; small and early-stage co
 mpanies are encouraged.\n• Abstract and lay summary — Scientific abs
 tract plus a lay summary of max 250 words.\n• Research proposal — Se
 lf-contained case for support (background\, aims\, programme with milest
 ones\, potential impact): 1\,000 words in the form or a PDF of up to 2 p
 ages of A4 (Arial 10 or larger) in the 2026 notes\; if the PDRA is secon
 ded\, state each person's role and time.\n• Benefits and mechanism of 
 collaboration — Max 200 words each: mutual benefit to both organisatio
 ns (and to the PDRA)\, and how the secondment will run (days at the part
 ner\, other contact).\n• Current employer Head of Department support 
 — Submitted through Flexi-Grant.\n• Partner organisation Head of Dep
 artment support — Submitted through Flexi-Grant.\n• One nominated re
 feree — Someone able to comment independently on the application.\n•
  PDRA details (if the PDRA is seconded) — The PDRA's contract must cov
 er the whole fellowship.\n• Host organisation approval — University 
 approver must approve in Flexi-Grant by the deadline.\n\nhttps://royalso
 ciety.org/grants/short-industry-fellowships/
URL:https://royalsociety.org/grants/short-industry-fellowships/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Deadline — Short Industry Fellowship (Royal Society)
TRIGGER:-P7D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
