SUMMARY:Start preparing — Short Industry Fellowship (Royal Society)
DESCRIPTION:Effort: moderate (3-5 weeks elapsed).\n\nWhat you need:\n• 
 UK industry partner — Company with an established research team and fa
 cilities\; small and early-stage companies are encouraged.\n• Abstract
  and lay summary — Scientific abstract plus a lay summary of max 250 w
 ords.\n• Research proposal — Self-contained case for support (backgr
 ound\, aims\, programme with milestones\, potential impact): 1\,000 word
 s in the form or a PDF of up to 2 pages of A4 (Arial 10 or larger) in th
 e 2026 notes\; if the PDRA is seconded\, state each person's role and ti
 me.\n• Benefits and mechanism of collaboration — Max 200 words each:
  mutual benefit to both organisations (and to the PDRA)\, and how the se
 condment will run (days at the partner\, other contact).\n• Current em
 ployer Head of Department support — Submitted through Flexi-Grant.\n
 • Partner organisation Head of Department support — Submitted throug
 h Flexi-Grant.\n• One nominated referee — Someone able to comment in
 dependently on the application.\n• PDRA details (if the PDRA is second
 ed) — The PDRA's contract must cover the whole fellowship.\n• Host o
 rganisation approval — University approver must approve in Flexi-Grant
  by the deadline.\n\nhttps://royalsociety.org/grants/short-industry-fell
 owships/
