DTSTAMP:20261123T121712Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270402
SUMMARY:Start preparing (round expected\, dates not announced) — Intern
 ational Exchanges (Royal Society)
DESCRIPTION:Effort: light (3-4 weeks elapsed).\n\nWhat you need:\n• Ove
 rseas co-applicant (new collaboration) — Co-applicant must hold a PhD 
 and a contract covering the project and cannot be a former colleague or 
 PhD student/supervisor. The UK applicant starts the application on behal
 f of both teams.\n• Abstract and lay summary — Scientific abstract m
 ax 400 words\; lay summary max 250 words (the panel is not all specialis
 ts).\n• Research proposal — Max 500 words\, including methods and te
 chniques.\n• Participants and benefits sections — Participants max 2
 00 words\; benefits to individuals/institutions\, to the UK and to the o
 verseas country max 200 words each.\n• Applicant and co-applicant care
 er summaries — Completed by each lead in Flexi-Grant (field of special
 isation max 20 words\; current research max 200 words).\n• Head of Dep
 artment support (UK and overseas) — Both Heads of Department confirm s
 upport through Flexi-Grant\, ideally at least 5 working days before the 
 deadline.\n• Visit plan and budget — Travel\, subsistence and resear
 ch expenses within the cap for the chosen duration\; multi-visit awards 
 must be bilateral.\n• Data management and sharing plan — Max 200 wor
 ds.\n• Host organisation approval — University approver must approve
  in Flexi-Grant by the deadline. For Cost Share rounds the overseas part
 ner submits a parallel application to its own funder.\n\nhttps://royalso
 ciety.org/grants/international-exchanges/
URL:https://royalsociety.org/grants/international-exchanges/
