SUMMARY:Start preparing (round expected\, dates not announced) — ERC St
 arting Grant (European Research Council)
DESCRIPTION:Effort: major (4-5 months part-time).\n\nWhat you need:\n• 
 Part I of the scientific proposal — Up to 5 pages\; with the CV it is 
 all the panel assesses at step 1.\n• CV and track record — Up to 4 p
 ages.\n• Part II of the scientific proposal — Up to 7 pages: detaile
 d methodology\, risks and background.\n• Resources and time commitment
  — Up to 2 pages\; minimum 50% of your working time on the project.\n
 • Host Institution Support Letter — Binding statement of support fro
 m the University\; proposals without the required sections may be declar
 ed inadmissible.\n• PhD certificate and eligibility evidence — Proof
  of the PhD defence date\, plus documents for any extension claimed.\n
 • Administrative forms and ethics self-assessment — Completed online
  in the EU Funding & Tenders Portal.\n• Step-2 interview — Shortlist
 ed PIs present their proposal to the evaluation panel.\n\nhttps://erc.eu
 ropa.eu/apply-grant/starting-grant
