SUMMARY:Start preparing (round expected\, dates not announced) — Explor
 ing the frontiers of environmental research 2026 (NERC)
DESCRIPTION:Effort: moderate (2-3 weeks part-time).\n\nWhat you need:\n
 • Remit check with NERC — The research must sit predominantly within
  NERC's research areas and address a clearly defined environmental scien
 ce question\; NERC encourages you to contact it first if the idea may cr
 oss council boundaries.\n• Internal quality assurance at Manchester 
 — NERC strongly recommends an institutional quality-assurance step\; y
 ou may appear on at most two applications and lead only one.\n• Summar
 y — 550 words\, in plain English.\n• Core team and discipline areas 
 — List team members by role\; name up to five discipline areas from NE
 RC's list (50 words).\n• Vision — 1\,200 words.\n• Approach\, and 
 ethics and responsible research and innovation — Both are assessment a
 reas\; their word limits are not shown in the brief — confirm in the g
 uidance.\n• Costing through the research office — £100\,000–£200
 \,000 full economic cost at 80%\; at least 0.2 FTE of your own time\; no
  PhD studentships\, no equipment item over £25\,000 and no data archivi
 ng costs.\n• Facility agreement\, if needed — Prior agreement and a 
 technical assessment from any NERC facility\; ship-time\, marine equipme
 nt and HPC have their own access rules and must fit within the grant lim
 it.\n• Research office submission on the UKRI Funding Service — Only
  the lead research organisation can submit\; allow for internal deadline
 s.\n• Reviewer commitment (distributed peer review) — Review about s
 ix to eight other applications within 15 working days\; in the 2026 roun
 d the window is 6–27 January 2027\, and missing it means automatic rej
 ection.\n\nhttps://www.ukri.org/opportunity/exploring-the-frontiers-of-e
 nvironmental-research-2026/
URL:https://www.ukri.org/opportunity/exploring-the-frontiers-of-environme
 ntal-research-2026/
